// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 11-initialization
// facility: [T-Let-Destructure] (D-0044); conf.destructure-not-a-struct-rejected
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.unbound-name (static)
//
// `q { x } = q;`, `q` a local: the statement is a destructuring by its
// shape (spec/22 disambiguation (5)), and no struct is named `q`. Before
// CHG-0347 the parser required a known type name there and reported a
// syntax error.

import std;

fn main()
{
    i32 q = 1;
    q { x } = q;
    printf("%v\n", x);
}
